Changes are listed newest first. Display name: Legs (decided October 15, 2026); the code prefix
stays NimbyAutorun.

Changes made for the NIMBY | HARDCORE | BADLANDS | 1pp server, October 20, 2026 (Legs plan
decision A8, DayZ 1.30):
- stopOnSwim now defaults to false: autorun carries into water and keeps swimming until a stop
  input (any Shift press, W, A, S, D), a menu, or a server clear ends it; fast swim drains
  stamina and drops to the slower stroke the way sprint drops to run. The October 19 dam run
  proved the movement override drives the swim command. A server that wants water to stop
  autorun sets "stopOnSwim": 1 in $profile:NimbyAutorun\config.json; existing files keep
  their own value.

Changes made for the NIMBY | HARDCORE | BADLANDS | 1pp server, October 20, 2026 (Legs plan
round 4, DayZ 1.30):
- With stopOnSwim false, the vanilla swimming input exclude no longer counts as disabled
  controls. Vanilla adds it on every swim start and it blocks only the weapon raise, but it
  made the October 19 run stop with cause=control-disabled on entering water. Any other
  exclude, any restriction, or the legacy disable still stops autorun and refuses a start; with
  stopOnSwim true (the default) nothing changes.

Changes made for the NIMBY | HARDCORE | BADLANDS | 1pp server, October 20, 2026 (Legs plan
round 3, DayZ 1.30):
- Data/Inputs.xml now declares the nimby sorting group inside <inputs>; bindings appear under
  a NIMBY tab in Options > Controls (NIMBY-T-007, proven October 19, 2026).
- Swim experiment (NIMBY-T-006): new config.json key stopOnSwim, default true. True keeps the
  earlier behavior (autorun stops on entering water and does not start while swimming); false
  lets autorun carry on into the water. The server sends the value to the owning client with
  the new RPC 6550103 on every start. A debug line marks each swim start and end while
  autorun is on. config.json moves to version 2; a version 1 file is rewritten once with the
  new key, keeping its other values.
- The forced-clear line on disconnect or removal names the player again: the name, BI id, and
  Steam64 are kept from connect and from each request, because the identity can be gone by the
  time the removal hook runs (NIMBY-T-005).
- The config line at server start is always written and shows requestsPerSecond and
  stopOnSwim.

Changes made for the NIMBY | HARDCORE | BADLANDS | 1pp server, October 19, 2026 (Legs plan
round 2 after the solo block, DayZ 1.30):
- Players who ran a build before October 19, 2026 keep their old binding (numpad plus); reset
  "Legs: toggle autorun" to default in Options > Controls > Others to get the double tap.
- After sprint drops to run because stamina ran out, autorun returns to sprint once vanilla
  would let a held Shift sprint again. It stays at walk or run if the player chose that speed
  with Left Ctrl, until the next start.
- A double tap while the weapon is raised does not start autorun; lower the weapon and double-tap
  again.

Changes made for the NIMBY | HARDCORE | BADLANDS | 1pp server, October 19, 2026 (Legs plan
Phase 1, DayZ 1.30):
- Default key is a double tap of Left Shift instead of numpad plus, listed in Options >
  Controls > Others as "Legs: toggle autorun" so players can rebind it.
- Autorun stops when the player takes control back: any Shift press, W, A, S, D, Space (jump
  or vault), fire, weapon raise, lean, or the toggle. The second press of a double tap that
  stopped autorun does not start it again. Chat, gestures, and the radial quickbar do not stop
  it. Shift no longer selects sprint while running.
- Focus loss, a dialog, the inventory, the pause menu, any other input-capturing menu,
  disabled controls, a ladder, and water stop autorun; it never resumes on its own.
- Client state resets on respawn, player replacement, disconnect, and mission teardown.
- New server-to-client RPC 6550102: the server tells the owning client to stop on every
  forced clear and every refused request, and the client does not re-send start.
- Server clears autorun itself on vehicle entry, unconsciousness, restraint, death, disconnect,
  and deletion, and drops sprint to run when the player can no longer sprint.
- Server limits requests to 10 per second per player (config.json requestsPerSecond); a stop
  is never limited. Ownership is checked before the payload is read.
- Validation, the request limit, and the stop rules moved to engine-free classes with a
  self-test. Logs carry the BI id and the Steam64 id; toggle lines only with the debug flag.
- Movement overrides use the 1.30 HumanInputControllerOverrideType values.

Changes made for the NIMBY | HARDCORE | BADLANDS | 1pp server, October 14, 2026:
- Renamed the addon, classes, members, input action, and RPC id to the Nimby prefix so the
  fork cannot collide with the original if both are loaded.
- Server now validates the autorun RPC: the sender must own the player entity, the movement
  index and angle must be in range, sprint is refused when the player cannot sprint, and the
  request is refused while the player is in a vehicle, unconscious, restrained, or dead.
- Rejected requests are logged to the server script log, rate-limited per player.
- The client sends an autorun update only when the running state or speed changes. The original sent
  a guaranteed RPC every frame while the player could not sprint (review CR-004, October 14, 2026).
